    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Across the whole packet, policy debate follows one dominant pattern shown by the cited source.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_2041657d5649d519\",\"quote\":\"As the DUP’s home affairs spokesman, I say gently that this evening’s statement would have been stronger if Members had been less selective in their condemnation of political commentary and abuse. Just today, I received notification from a local PSNI inspector in east Belfast that abuse reported to him could not be progressed because Twitter does not comply or engage unless there…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_a5ba0b854db8a8a6\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, I am going to respond but I will have to let the noble Lord draw his own conclusions as to how positive the response is. My noble and learned friend Lord Mackay has raised an interesting point and I thank him. In the interests of discipline and autonomy, and respecting the Haldane principle, it is right that the council should have special delegated authority to appoint…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_7d20d54bc5b171dd\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, I support Amendment 17, moved by the noble Lord, Lord Pannick, which is linked to Amendment 35, standing in my name. Amendment 17 is critically important. If there is no clarity tonight, we should certainly return to this subject on Report next week In fact, the amendment arose from the end of one of the banks of debates on Monday night, when I asked the Minister—this is…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_dd009f72fe33a113\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, I beg leave to ask the Question standing in my name on the Order Paper. In doing so, I refer to my register entry as a solicitor.”}],\"\n        },{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_7d20d54bc5b171dd\",\"quote\":\"The Minister refused to respond or give any indication of the Government’s intentions. He now has a chance to make clear beyond doubt the Government’s position, which the House has the right to know. The best way to achieve this would be to accept Amendment 17 or, if that cannot be carried, by insisting on Amendment 35 which provides that if the UK Government fail to reach…\"},\n        {\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_2041657d5649d519\",\"quote\":\"...abuse reported to him could not be progressed because Twitter does not comply or engage unless there is an imminent threat to life.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"The cited source does not demonstrate a single dominant pattern across the whole packet of policy debate.\",\"mechanism\":\"The claims present distinct debates unrelated to a single dominant pattern.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely asserts a unified pattern where none exists, obscuring the diverse and specific concerns raised in the provided excerpts.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The excerpts represent separate debates concerning police investigations, legislative provisions, and amendment proposals, lacking a common overarching pattern.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence demonstrates a lack of a single dominant pattern across the provided excerpts, undermining the initial claim. The excerpts cover distinct policy areas and concerns, indicating a fragmented debate landscape.\"}",
